{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GjNKLZ98YTwdxkLFXyfbmu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Run review queue fixture\n2\t\n3\tA dependency-free, in-memory review queue for benchmark runs. The fixture has\n4\tthree layers:\n5\t\n6\t- `review-store.mjs` — in-memory store (`createReviewStore`) keeping at most\n7\t  one current review per `runId`.\n8\t- `review-api.mjs` — synchronous JSON-style API boundary (`createReviewApi`)\n9\t  returning `{ status, headers, body }` responses.\n10\t- `review-page.mjs` — server-rendered HTML page (`renderReviewPage`) with a\n11\t  summary, a review form, and a table of saved reviews.\n12\t\n13\t## Routes\n14\t\n15\t### `POST /api/reviews`\n16\t\n17\tSaves the current review for a run. Posting again for the same `runId`\n18\treplaces the stored review while preserving its `createdAt` timestamp.\n19\t\n20\t- The body must be an object with exactly the string fields `runId`,\n21\t  `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`. Any other field is reported as a sorted\n22\t  `body` field error (for example `Unknown fields: alpha, zeta`).\n23\t- All four values are trimmed before validation and storage.\n24\t- `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n25\t- `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n26\t- `reviewer` must contain 2 through 40 characters after trimming.\n27\t- `note` may be at most 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n28\t  `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n29\t- Returns `201` with `{ review }` for a new run and `200` with `{ review }`\n30\t  for an update. Reviews carry `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, `note`,\n31\t  `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`.\n32\t- Invalid input returns `400` with\n33\t  `{ \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": { ... } }` listing every detected\n34\t  problem; nothing is saved.\n35\t\n36\t### `GET /api/reviews`\n37\t\n38\tReturns `{ reviews, summary }`. Reviews are sorted by newest `updatedAt`\n39\tfirst, breaking timestamp ties by lexicographically smaller `runId`. The\n40\t`summary` always counts all stored reviews and has exactly `total`,\n41\t`approve`, `reject`, and `needs-work`. An optional `?decision=` query filters\n42\tonly the `reviews` array; an invalid decision value returns the standard\n43\t`validation_failed` error.\n44\t\n45\t### `GET /api/reviews/:runId`\n46\t\n47\tReturns `200` with `{ review }`, or `404` with\n48\t`{ \"error\": \"review_not_found\" }` when the run has no review.\n49\t\n50\t## Errors and headers\n51\t\n52\tEvery response has exactly the shape `{ status, headers, body }` and includes\n53\tthe header `content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n54\t\n55\t- `400 { \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": { ... } }` — invalid input;\n56\t  nothing is saved.\n57\t- `400 { \"error\": \"invalid_request\" }` — unusable request object or URL.\n58\t- `404 { \"error\": \"not_found\" }` — unknown route.\n59\t- `404 { \"error\": \"review_not_found\" }` — unknown run id on a detail route.\n60\t- `405 { \"error\": \"method_not_allowed\" }` — unsupported method on a recognized\n61\t  route. Includes an `allow` header: `GET, POST` on the collection and `GET`\n62\t  on a detail route.\n63\t\n64\t## Storage limits\n65\t\n66\tThe store is process-local and not durable: reviews live only in memory, so\n67\tthe store resets on every process restart. It has no external dependencies\n68\tand no persistence layer.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c56c70be-17cd-4219-9f0a-e7eecfb0e52e","uuid":"92a21b52-a007-466d-bf5c-76e373a216b3","timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:01:52.796Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-workflow-o0L2GK/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md","content":"# Run review queue fixture\n\nA dependency-free, in-memory review queue for benchmark runs. The fixture has\nthree layers:\n\n- `review-store.mjs` — in-memory store (`createReviewStore`) keeping at most\n  one current review per `runId`.\n- `review-api.mjs` — synchronous JSON-style API boundary (`createReviewApi`)\n  returning `{ status, headers, body }` responses.\n- `review-page.mjs` — server-rendered HTML page (`renderReviewPage`) with a\n  summary, a review form, and a table of saved reviews.\n\n## Routes\n\n### `POST /api/reviews`\n\nSaves the current review for a run. Posting again for the same `runId`\nreplaces the stored review while preserving its `createdAt` timestamp.\n\n- The body must be an object with exactly the string fields `runId`,\n  `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`. Any other field is reported as a sorted\n  `body` field error (for example `Unknown fields: alpha, zeta`).\n- All four values are trimmed before validation and storage.\n- `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n- `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n- `reviewer` must contain 2 through 40 characters after trimming.\n- `note` may be at most 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n  `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n- Returns `201` with `{ review }` for a new run and `200` with `{ review }`\n  for an update. Reviews carry `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, `note`,\n  `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`.\n- Invalid input returns `400` with\n  `{ \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": { ... } }` listing every detected\n  problem; nothing is saved.\n\n### `GET /api/reviews`\n\nReturns `{ reviews, summary }`. Reviews are sorted by newest `updatedAt`\nfirst, breaking timestamp ties by lexicographically smaller `runId`. The\n`summary` always counts all stored reviews and has exactly `total`,\n`approve`, `reject`, and `needs-work`. An optional `?decision=` query filters\nonly the `reviews` array; an invalid decision value returns the standard\n`validation_failed` error.\n\n### `GET /api/reviews/:runId`\n\nReturns `200` with `{ review }`, or `404` with\n`{ \"error\": \"review_not_found\" }` when the run has no review.\n\n## Errors and headers\n\nEvery response has exactly the shape `{ status, headers, body }` and includes\nthe header `content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8`.\n\n- `400 { \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": { ... } }` — invalid input;\n  nothing is saved.\n- `400 { \"error\": \"invalid_request\" }` — unusable request object or URL.\n- `404 { \"error\": \"not_found\" }` — unknown route.\n- `404 { \"error\": \"review_not_found\" }` — unknown run id on a detail route.\n- `405 { \"error\": \"method_not_allowed\" }` — unsupported method on a recognized\n  route. Includes an `allow` header: `GET, POST` on the collection and `GET`\n  on a detail route.\n\n## Storage limits\n\nThe store is process-local and not durable: reviews live only in memory, so\nthe store resets on every process restart. It has no external dependencies\nand no persistence layer.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
