{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GbKnytYtauo8Mw2hgvgFqT","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md b/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md\nindex bb59cf2..3596b6d 100644\n--- a/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md\n+++ b/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md\n@@ -1,3 +1,68 @@\n # Run review queue fixture\n \n-TODO: document the completed feature, API behavior, and operating limits.\n+A dependency-free, in-memory review queue for benchmark runs. The fixture has\n+three layers:\n+\n+- `review-store.mjs` — in-memory store (`createReviewStore`) keeping at most\n+  one current review per `runId`.\n+- `review-api.mjs` — synchronous JSON-style API boundary (`createReviewApi`)\n+  returning `{ status, headers, body }` responses.\n+- `review-page.mjs` — server-rendered HTML page (`renderReviewPage`) with a\n+  summary, a review form, and a table of saved reviews.\n+\n+## Routes\n+\n+### `POST /api/reviews`\n+\n+Saves the current review for a run. Posting again for the same `runId`\n+replaces the stored review while preserving its `createdAt` timestamp.\n+\n+- The body must be an object with exactly the string fields `runId`,\n+  `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`. Any other field is reported as a sorted\n+  `body` field error (for example `Unknown fields: alpha, zeta`).\n+- All four values are trimmed before validation and storage.\n+- `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n+- `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n+- `reviewer` must contain 2 through 40 characters after trimming.\n+- `note` may be at most 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n+  `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n+- Returns `201` with `{ review }` for a new run and `200` with `{ review }`\n+  for an update. Reviews carry `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, `note`,\n+  `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`.\n+- Invalid input returns `400` with\n+  `{ \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": { ... } }` listing every detected\n+  problem; nothing is saved.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c56c70be-17cd-4219-9f0a-e7eecfb0e52e","uuid":"9c43d711-5dae-432e-87d2-865a063bb679","timestamp":"2026-08-23T18:03:23.452Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md b/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md\nindex bb59cf2..3596b6d 100644\n--- a/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md\n+++ b/benchmark/fixtures/T5-review-queue/README.md\n@@ -1,3 +1,68 @@\n # Run review queue fixture\n \n-TODO: document the completed feature, API behavior, and operating limits.\n+A dependency-free, in-memory review queue for benchmark runs. The fixture has\n+three layers:\n+\n+- `review-store.mjs` — in-memory store (`createReviewStore`) keeping at most\n+  one current review per `runId`.\n+- `review-api.mjs` — synchronous JSON-style API boundary (`createReviewApi`)\n+  returning `{ status, headers, body }` responses.\n+- `review-page.mjs` — server-rendered HTML page (`renderReviewPage`) with a\n+  summary, a review form, and a table of saved reviews.\n+\n+## Routes\n+\n+### `POST /api/reviews`\n+\n+Saves the current review for a run. Posting again for the same `runId`\n+replaces the stored review while preserving its `createdAt` timestamp.\n+\n+- The body must be an object with exactly the string fields `runId`,\n+  `decision`, `reviewer`, and `note`. Any other field is reported as a sorted\n+  `body` field error (for example `Unknown fields: alpha, zeta`).\n+- All four values are trimmed before validation and storage.\n+- `runId` must match `^run-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{2,63}$`.\n+- `decision` must be `approve`, `reject`, or `needs-work`.\n+- `reviewer` must contain 2 through 40 characters after trimming.\n+- `note` may be at most 240 characters and is required for `reject` and\n+  `needs-work`; it may be empty for `approve`.\n+- Returns `201` with `{ review }` for a new run and `200` with `{ review }`\n+  for an update. Reviews carry `runId`, `decision`, `reviewer`, `note`,\n+  `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`.\n+- Invalid input returns `400` with\n+  `{ \"error\": \"validation_failed\", \"fields\": { ... } }` listing every detected\n+  problem; nothing is saved.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
